      { "target": "Tumefungwa leo.", "base": "We lost today." },
      { "target": "Tucheze karata!", "base": "Let’s play cards!" }
    ],
    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "ku-to",
        "title": "Ku-: to do, doing",
        "body": [
          "The plain form of a verb starts with **ku-**: **kuimba** (to sing), **kuogelea** (to swim), **kuangalia** (to watch). After **ninapenda** it means “-ing”: **Ninapenda kuimba** (I like singing).",
          "**Kucheza** covers playing and dancing: **kucheza mpira** (to play football), **kucheza karata** (to play cards), **kucheza ngoma** (to dance)."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "Simba and Yanga",
        "body": [
          "In Dar es Salaam, nearly everyone supports **Simba** or **Young Africans** (Yanga), and the Kariakoo derby stops the city. In Kenya, the big rivalry is **Gor Mahia** against **AFC Leopards**."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Bongo flava",
        "body": ["**Bongo flava** is Tanzanian pop: hip hop, R&B and taarab sung in Swahili. Its stars are famous all over Africa."]
      }
    ]
  },
